{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1001342-a-couple-queries-concerning-namely-matter","id":1001342,"title":"A couple queries concerning namely Matter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-10T07:03:16-08:00","id":1001342,"title":"A couple queries concerning namely Matter","content":"I'm looking for some additional opinions as to what some of the board might think regarding a few matter effects/spells. A couple of these have come up during some recent sessions and I'd like to make sure I'm handling them consistently with how the system is meant to handle them or at least conceptual consistent.<br /> <br /> Matter 3 (State Change) Rote Skill: Craft<br /> <br /> 3 Dice to cast the spell after penalties (Gnosis 1, Matter 3, Craft 3)<br /> 3 reach due to Rote (1 reach - Instant Cast, 1 reach - gas to solid, 1 reach - advanced scale (large house))<br /> 1 Mana to activate Permanence from matter 2 attainment so spell lasts 1 hour<br /> EDIT: -4 dice to kick up potency (forgot to note)<br /> <br /> It seems this spell can effectively suffocate an entire building; not by solidifying the air in lungs mind you but by not allowing any air into the building for an hour. The spell wasn't used for this in game but it was a point that was brought up after the fact. Does that seem correct?<br /> <br /> Matter 3 (Wonderful Machine)<br /> <br /> Have you lot had this spell actually smash the two items together, creating an amalgam of the objects/devices? Just had it swap the pieces of objects together, resulting in 2 broken items once the spell ends? Just had the property of one item stop working until the spell ends?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5951,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5951-cayros","user":"Cayros","date":". 11-10-2016, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5951-cayros","name":"Cayros","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T07:22:45-08:00","id":1001346,"title":"","content":"I think you would need another Reach to turn State Change from Touch to Sensory, unless you were in the house when you cast it. Otherwise that seems fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T08:46:47-08:00","id":1001369,"title":"","content":"Wonderful Machine: It's vague enough to just leave up to the ST. I don't see a reason to punish it by making the components fall apart and be useless after the spell ends though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:33:42-08:00","id":1001493,"title":"","content":"I did a quick research on the subject, out of curiosity, and the first spell won't actually do much. It will probably take much more than an hour to actually hurt people inside the building, unless it is really overcrowded by very active athletes, and when I say overcrowded, I mean it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:38:26-08:00","id":1001498,"title":"","content":"Funny enough, there's a sidebar in the Space spells that lays out the volume of air a human body at rest consumes (at least for Mage rules purposes). So that kind of spell has been explicitly accounted for within the rules and encouraged! You'd need a fairly long duration though. Maybe use another Matter spell to seal the doors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T15:01:45-08:00","id":1001509,"title":"","content":"Why not move the air out of the building? It would be like Matter Rulling spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T15:03:14-08:00","id":1001513,"title":"","content":"I don't believe solidified air would be much of a deterrent, anyhow. You would need to up the Potency, as otherwise the Durability of the new solid is 1, which isn't too tough. <br /> <br /> That said it is easy to kill Sleepers and fortunately doing so doesn't offer Experience on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T16:28:12-08:00","id":1001539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1001342-a-couple-queries-concerning-namely-matter?p=1001513#post1001513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said it is easy to kill Sleepers and fortunately doing so doesn't offer Experience on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as you don't have it as aspiration or obsesion. Aren't acts of hubris grant beats?<br /> <br /> Also just Shielding everybody from oxygen would do the trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T19:00:23-08:00","id":1001586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1001342-a-couple-queries-concerning-namely-matter?p=1001539#post1001539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't acts of hubris grant beats?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, which is why I added the qualifier 'on its own.'<br /> <br /> Each human is not worth their Integrity in Beats to kill, for instance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also just Shielding everybody from oxygen would do the trick. </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's easy to kill Sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}